{
  "id": "ALAS2023-2026-2029",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2023 - ALAS2023-2026-2029: Important priority package update for pipewire",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-08-03 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-08-03 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-5674:\n\tA flaw was found in PipeWire, a multimedia server. This vulnerability allows an attacker to escape sandboxed applications, such as Flatpak, by exploiting PipeWire's PulseAudio compatibility layer. An attacker with minimal permissions within a sandboxed environment can load a malicious library, leading to arbitrary code execution outside the sandbox and potential compromise of the user's system.\n\nCVE-2026-14330:\n\tMultiple unbounded alloca() calls in the PulseAudio protocol server.\n\nCVE-2026-14324:\n\tRAOP module accepts unbounded Content-Length values and does not check the pw_array_add() return.\n",
